From: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] nss-drv: preserve skb allocation truesize for frag lists

NSS assembles multi-buffer linear packets as skb frag lists. Keep the
allocation truesize of the head and account the full allocation of each
chained skb instead of replacing both values with payload lengths.

Under-accounting these skbs can trigger the delta < len warning in
skb_try_coalesce() when a chained TCP packet reaches the receive queue.

Signed-off-by: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>
---
--- a/nss_core.c
+++ b/nss_core.c
@@ -1385,7 +1385,6 @@
 
 		skb_frag_list_init(nbuf);
 		nbuf->data_len = 0;
-		nbuf->truesize = desc->payload_len;
 		nbuf->priority = desc->pri;
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_NET_CLS_ACT
@@ -1445,7 +1444,7 @@
 	 */
 	head->data_len += desc->payload_len;
 	head->len += desc->payload_len;
-	head->truesize += desc->payload_len;
+	head->truesize += nbuf->truesize;
 
 	if (!(bit_flags & N2H_BIT_FLAG_LAST_SEGMENT)) {
 		/*
